  "long_biography": {
    "plain_text": "Physician Scott Burke joined a Colorado medical team in Haiti after the 2010 earthquake. Working in a makeshift operating room in Port-au-Prince, he helped provide emergency surgery with limited equipment. The team faced shortages of sterile clothing and intravenous supplies, while some donated gloves were too old to use.\n\nThe experience sharpened his concern with getting supplies to the people treating patients. He praised the coordination of relief organisations that moved equipment rapidly from aircraft to hospitals. He also described the gratitude of a patient’s father, who gave him a cloth bracelet after the team treated his daughter.",
    "html": "<p>Physician Scott Burke joined a Colorado medical team in Haiti after the 2010 earthquake. Working in a makeshift operating room in Port-au-Prince, he helped provide emergency surgery with limited equipment. The team faced shortages of sterile clothing and intravenous supplies, while some donated gloves were too old to use.</p>\r\n<p>The experience sharpened his concern with getting supplies to the people treating patients. He praised the coordination of relief organisations that moved equipment rapidly from aircraft to hospitals. He also described the gratitude of a patient’s father, who gave him a cloth bracelet after the team treated his daughter.</p>\r\n",
    "word_count": 98,
